# The square tour: 600 mm sides, CCW, axis-aligned, with planned stops
# mid-leg on legs 1 and 3.
#
# AXIS-ALIGNED means each leg runs along one axis of the tour's own
# start frame: leg 1 all +x, leg 2 all +y, and so on. It always did --
# but until 2026-09-01 the chart drew it as a DIAMOND, because the plot
# was in the robot's raw odometry frame and nothing on the wire can
# rebase that frame between tours (see the issue
# no-wire-verb-reaches-rebaseposition-...). MEASURED gopiv 2026-09-01,
# reports/tours-20260901/square.json: the run started at (-1154, -208)
# mm with a cumulative heading of 4909.66 deg = 229.66 deg, and the
# first leg travelled at -130.19 deg -- the same direction. Re-rendered
# in the start frame it is a 30.4 x 30.2 cm square with its first leg
# at +0.15 deg. run_tour.py now always charts in the start frame.
# For a figure that is genuinely turned 45 deg, see diamond.tour.
#
# SIZING. 600 mm sides span 600 x 600 mm; the usable field is
# +-600 x +-400 mm and the working budget +-550 x +-350 (tours/FIELD.md),
# so 600 is the largest round side that fits the tight (y) axis.
# Stage the robot at (-300, -300) facing East to sit centred -- driven
# from the field CENTRE this square reaches +600 mm and does not fit.
#
# PIVOT SPEED. omega=180 deg/s, not the 45 deg/s this file was ported
# with. 45 deg/s works out to 47 mm/s at the wheel, which is at the
# stiction floor: MEASURED gopiv 2026-09-01 the pivots took 4.5-5.0 s
# each, ran a median 46 mm/s, and chattered raggedly between 0 and
# 75 mm/s while the straights held a clean 144 mm/s. 180 deg/s is
# ~188 mm/s at the wheel, matching the straights -- and it also turns
# out to be the accurate speed, not just the clean-sounding one (see
# the pivot tuning note below).

# PIVOT TUNING (MEASURED gopiv 2026-09-01, interleaved A/B so battery
# drift hits both arms equally). Pivot cruise 188 mm/s (omega 180 deg/s)
# beats 300 mm/s (286 deg/s) decisively: excess +1.34 deg sd 0.35 versus
# +6.88 deg sd 1.03, n=8 each. pivot_overrun was then swept AT 188 mm/s
# and 0.68 -- the value the closure sweep found at 300 mm/s -- leaves
# +1.44 deg on the table; 2.0 is the zero crossing (1.8 -> +0.29,
# 2.2 -> -0.25). pivot_overrun is speed-dependent: retune it whenever
# the pivot cruise changes.

SET twist_hold_gain 8
SET speed_floor 512
SET yaw_taper 800
SET pivot_overrun 2.0

MARK leg1a
TWIST vx=250 dist=300 timeout=6
STOP dwell=0.6
MARK leg1b
TWIST vx=250 dist=300 timeout=6
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6

MARK leg2
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6

MARK leg3a
TWIST vx=250 dist=300 timeout=6
STOP dwell=0.6
MARK leg3b
TWIST vx=250 dist=300 timeout=6
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6

MARK leg4
TWIST vx=250 dist=600 timeout=8
TWIST omega=180 angle=90 timeout=6
STOP dwell=0.5
